<BaseLayout title="Research Peptides for Laboratories — Documentation & Sample Supply" description="Research peptide supply for academic and private laboratories: batch-linked COA, HPLC/MS data, sample lots, handling guidance and documented bulk supply." canonical="/applications/laboratories/">
  <div class="wrap-narrow">
    <p class="breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> › Applications › Laboratories</p>
    <h1>Research peptides for laboratories</h1>
    <div class="quick-answer"><strong>Quick answer.</strong> Laboratories need three things from a peptide supplier: a batch-linked COA with chromatogram and MS, a sample lot that matches the shipment, and handling data that survives an audit. Price is fourth.</div>
    <p class="lead muted">We supply academic, institutional and private laboratories that need documentation they can file, not just a vial with a label.</p>

    <h2>What we provide</h2>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Need</th><th>What you receive</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>Identity and purity</td><td>Batch COA with HPLC chromatogram, method and MS confirmation</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Traceability</td><td>Lot number linking vial, COA and invoice</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Sample before volume</td><td>Qualification sample with its own batch COA</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Handling</td><td>Storage and reconstitution notes; SDS where required</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Repeat supply</td><td>Consecutive lot data on request; retention samples per agreement</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2>How labs usually start</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Send a short list: compound, strength, quantity, destination.</li>
      <li>Review the sample COA for the lot we propose.</li>
      <li>Order a sample and run it through your own workflow.</li>
      <li>Move to a standing order with defined acceptance criteria.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>Documentation discipline</h2>
    <p>We do not send a generic product COA and call it batch data. The COA you receive should let you answer: which lot, tested how, by whom, with what result. If it cannot, ask us — or any supplier — for the missing piece before you order.</p>
    <p>For method and interpretation guidance, see the <a href="/knowledge/peptide-quality-verification-framework/">quality verification pillar</a> and <a href="/knowledge/peptide-handling-laboratory-practice/">handling pillar</a>.</p>

    <h2>Products commonly requested</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><a href="/products/research/">Research peptides</a> — BPC-157, TB-500, CJC-1295, Ipamorelin and more</li>
      <li><a href="/products/tirzepatide/">Tirzepatide</a> and <a href="/products/semaglutide/">Semaglutide</a> — reference materials</li>
      <li><a href="/products/accessories/bacteriostatic-water-10ml/">Bacteriostatic water</a> — reconstitution workflows</li>
    </ul>


    <h2>What we do not do</h2>
    <p>We do not provide dosing guidance, clinical protocols or product-use recommendations. We do not sell to individual consumers, and we decline requests that describe personal human use. If your project needs a compound we do not list, ask — custom synthesis is possible, but the specification conversation comes first.</p>

    <h2>Preparing your first order</h2>
    <p>Send the compound, strength, quantity and destination. We will reply with the lot we propose, its COA and the lead time. If the lot is not yet produced, we tell you that instead of quoting a date we cannot hold. For repeat work, agree the specification annex and the retention-sample arrangement before the second order — those two documents prevent most later disputes.</p>

    <h2>A note on incoming testing</h2>
    <p>Your incoming test is the final control, not a duplicate of ours. Sample the lot you received, record the vial and COA batch numbers, and keep a retention sample. If your result differs from the certificate, that comparison is the evidence both sides need — without it, the conversation becomes an opinion.</p>


    <h2>If something arrives wrong</h2>
    <p>Photograph the packaging before unpacking, keep the vial and the COA together, and contact us within the claim window. We will ask for the lot number, the receiving date and your observation. If the issue is document-related, we can usually resolve it without a return; if it is material-related, the retention sample decides the conversation.</p>

    <p><a class="btn" href="/contact/">Request a laboratory quotation</a> <a class="wa-btn" href={site.whatsappLink} target="_blank" rel="noopener" style="margin-left:10px;">💬 WhatsApp</a></p>
    <div class="ruo">{site.ruo}</div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
